.TITLE  ERMES


;       AOS/VS ERROR MESSAGE FILE GENERATOR


;  GROUP TABLE

;       THE GROUP TABLE CONSISTS OF 20000 2-DWORD ENTRIES (1 FOR
;       EACH GROUP). THE FIRST DWORD OF EACH ENTRY CONTAINS THE
;       WORD ADDRESS OF THE CORRESPONDING CODE VECTOR.  THE
;       SECOND DWORD CONTAINS THE NUMBER OF CODES FOR THE 
;       GROUP (CODE VECTOR LENGTH).



;  GRP
;       THE MACRO 'GRP' IS USED TO DEFINE A GROUP.  IT FILLS THE
;       APPROPRIATE ENTRY IN THE GROUP TABLE AND ALLOCATES THE
;       CODE VECTOR FOR THE GROUP.

;       ARGUMENTS TO GRP MACRO:
;               ^1      GROUP NUMBER
;               ^2      MAXIMUM NUMBER OF CODES

        .MACRO  GRP
**      .PUSH   .RDX
**      .RDX    8
**
**      .TXTM   1
**      .TXTN   0
**      .NREL   0
**
**      G=      .               ;NREL REFERENCE
**      GROUP=  ^1*1000         ;DEFINE THE GROUP NUMBER
**      .LOC    4*^1            ;POSITION IN GROUP TABLE (ZREL)
        G                       ;WORD ADDR OF CODE VECTOR
        ^2                      ;MAX NUMBER OF CODES
**      .LOC    G               ;POSITION OF CODE VECTOR
**      .BLK    ^2*2            ;RESERVE CODE VECTOR
**      .RDX    .POP
**
%

;  CODE
;       THE MACRO 'CODE' IS USED TO INSERT AN ENTRY INTO THE
;       CURRENT CODE VECTOR.  IT SHOULD BE FOLLOWED BY A .TXT 
;       WITH ITS ERROR MESSAGE.

;       ARGUMENT OF CODE MACRO:
;               ^1      CODE NUMBER

        .MACRO  CODE
**
**      T=      .               ;NREL REFERENCE FOR TEXT
**      .LOC    (^1-GROUP)*2+G  ;POSITION IN CODE VECTOR
        T                       ;WORD ADDRESS OF TEXT
**      .LOC    T               ;REFERENCE TEXT
%



        .IFN    0




                                        ERRORS ONLY--DO NOT ACTUALLY ASSIGN
                                        CODES TO THIS GROUP NUMBER






        FORMAT FOR XXXERMES.SR FILES:

                .TITLE  XXXERMES

                GRP     GROUP NUMBER    MAXIMUM # OF ERROR CODES+2


                CODE    GRP.NUM. * 1000 + ERROR # (OR NOTE BELOW)
                .TXT    /AN ERROR MESSAGE TEXT STRING/

                [MORE ERROR CODES]

                .END

NOTE:
        SYMBOLIC NAMES CAN ALSO BE USED IN PLACE
        OF THE ARGUMENT (NUMBER * 1000 + ERROR #).
        THEY MUST ALSO BE ACCOMPANIED BY A 
        PARAMETER FILE PARXXX.SR.

        THE GRP MACRO DEFINES A SYMBOL "GROUP" WHICH IS
        EQUAL TO "GRP.NUM. * 1000" .
        GROUP MESSAGE FILES ARE ALLOCATED AS FOLLOWS:


                        "PARXXX"        "XXXERMES"

                0       PARDUMMY        SYSERMES
